      "content": "Running local LLM inference usually traps you in a massive dependency graph of Python runtimes, Torch packages, or vendor-locked CUDA toolkits. VindexLLM takes an unconventional route by implementing a complete GGUF transformer forward pass entirely in Delphi, driven by pure Vulkan compute shaders.\n\nAll heavy computations-from embedding lookups and 34 layers of attention to normalization and token sampling-execute through GLSL 450 shaders compiled to SPIR-V and embedded straight into the application binary. The only runtime requirement on Windows is the standard vulkan-1.dll bundled with modern graphics drivers.\n\nStripping away runtime layers changes how we think about edge deployment. By memory-mapping model files directly and dispatching shader pipelines natively, you avoid the memory footprint and startup overhead that plague typical inference servers.\n\nHardware portability does not have to mean accepting terrible performance. Clean compute shader architectures offer a viable path to fast, self-contained inference engines."
    },
    {
