      "content": "Running foundation models inside agent frameworks often degrades performance because each runtime harness imposes distinct tool definitions, control loops, and prompting patterns.\n\nHarness adapters solve this mismatch by fine-tuning lightweight LoRA adapters directly inside unmodified harnesses using reinforcement learning. Rather than retraining the underlying model from scratch, the system trains an adapter specifically tailored to the tools and interaction dynamics of targets like OpenCode or Hermes.\n\nA key design pattern here is the safeagents proxy, which intercepts every generated tool execution before dispatch. By validating commands against rule-based safety detectors, the training loop blocks reward-hacking attempts and scores them as zero.\n\nSmoke tests on held-out programming tasks demonstrate that adapter-tuned models consistently make fewer tool round-trips while matching or improving baseline completion rates.\n\nSpecializing lightweight adapters to execution harnesses produces far more reliable agent behavior than relying solely on prompting or massive monolithic models."
